---
title: Pasta Puttanesca
description: A spicy and flavorful pasta dish with a rich tomato-based sauce.
image: https://static01.nyt.com/images/2020/12/06/dining/15COOKING-PASTA/15COOKING-PASTA-superJumbo-v2.jpg?format=pjpg&quality=75&auto=webp&disable=upscale
source: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11583-pasta-puttanesca
servings: 4
---

= Sauce =

Warm 2 tablespoons of @olive oil{3%tbsp} with @garlic{3%cloves}(crushed) and @anchovy fillets{3} in a skillet over medium-low heat. Cook, stirring occasionally, until garlic is lightly golden.

Drain @whole plum tomatoes{1%can}(800g) and crush with a fork or your hands. Add to the skillet, along with some salt and @black pepper{}. Raise heat to medium-high and cook, stirring occasionally, until tomatoes break down and mixture becomes saucy, about ~{10%minutes}. 

Stir in @black olives{1/2%cup}, @capers{2%tbsp}, and @red pepper flakes{}, and continue to simmer.

= Pasta & Assembly =

Cook @linguine{1%lb}(450g), stirring occasionally, to al dente. 

Drain quickly and toss with the sauce and remaining 1 tablespoon of olive oil. 

Taste and adjust seasonings as necessary, garnish with @parsley{}(chopped) if you like, and serve.